  "body_html": "<h1>Threat Point</h1>\n<p>Let $G$ be a finite strategic game. The punishment level, or threat point, for\nplayer $i$ is\n$$\n  V_i=\n  \\min_{\\sigma_{-i}\\in\\prod_{j\\ne i}\\Delta(S_j)}\n  \\max_{s_i\\in S_i} g_i(s_i,\\sigma_{-i}).\n$$\nIt is the maximal punishment that the other players can enforce against player\n$i$ using independent mixed strategies.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 4.10.1] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. Punishment level or threat point in a finite strategic game.</li>\n</ul>",
